Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:14:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1042/1042] SableOS: Browser keys for the address bar, tabs,
 find and paging

Wire the Browser keyboard model into Jelly:

* WebClient.shouldOverrideKeyEvent takes the Alt (or Ctrl) chords
  before the page; WebClient.onUnhandledKeyEvent takes single keys
  only after the page declined them, so a page's own shortcuts keep
  working. MainActivity.onKeyDown covers keys while no page has focus.
* The input guard is WebView.onCheckIsTextEditor() (a focused web
  form) or the focused view (address bar, find).
* L / Alt+L focus the address field with its text selected; T / Alt+T
  open a new tab (private when the current tab is private); F, / and
  Alt+F open find in page; B and Alt+Left go back, Alt+Right forward;
  Alt+R reloads; Space and Shift+Space page with WebView.pageDown/
  pageUp; Move Home/End go to the top and bottom.
* A fullscreen video keeps its keys. Back and Esc keep their meaning
  (close find, then history back).
